WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.710
<v Instructor>So here comes a brief lecture</v>

2
00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.500
about AWS Service Quotas.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.440
So it's a service that helps you get notifications

4
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.910
when you're close to using a service quota value threshold.

5
00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.940
The idea is that you cannot abuse AWS services

6
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.100
and so there are safety quotas.

7
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.740
And when you approach them, so that you don't get throttled,

8
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.330
you can get notified.

9
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.640
For this, you can create CloudWatch alarms

10
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.490
directly on top of the Service Quotas console.

11
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.000
For example, you're looking for Lambda concurrent executions

12
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.170
and you want to get alerted

13
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.640
if you are about to approach a threshold, say of 100.

14
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.410
So it helps you know as well

15
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.510
if you need to request a quota increase

16
00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.270
or shut down resources before the limit is reached.

17
00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.910
So from the Service Quotas console,

18
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.460
you can create an alarm and it looks like this.

19
00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.070
So the Service Quota is going to monitor

20
00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.650
the AWS Lambda quota for concurrent executions

21
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.910
in this example.

22
00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:58.140
And in case we arrive at 9,000, which is a threshold we set,

23
00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.880
then we're going to trigger a CloudWatch alarm

24
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.770
and can get notified.

25
00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.750
So that's it, very simple architecture,

26
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.010
but one you should know.

27
00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.960
I hope you liked it and I will see you in the next lecture.

